# Infinity vs Kamuk — no mix

Kamuk and Infinity are **twins in product experience** (same Portal/Engine features: AI, games, KPIs, evaluation) but **separate projects**. Never merge them.

## Separation rules

| Concern | Infinity | Kamuk |
|---------|----------|-------|
| Repo / site | INFINTYSTUDIOCR/Database- · studioinfinitycr.com | KamukSchool/Operarive-Training-Database · GitHub Pages |
| Supabase | `rxruvpfd…` · tables `infinity_*` | `lbspgbeq…` · tables `kamuk_*` |
| Student IDs | `IS-…` | `KAM-…` |
| Student login | no product / infinity · `infinity_students` | `product: 'kamuk'` · `kamuk_students` only |
| Users/trainers | `infinity_users` | `kamuk_users` |
| Brand colors | Infinity purple | Kamuk blue (`#2B7EC1`) |

## Hard bans

- Never log a student into the other product’s tables as a “fallback”.
- Never write Infinity student rows into Kamuk Supabase, or Kamuk rows into Infinity.
- Never point Kamuk Portal/Engine `SUPA_URL` at Infinity Supabase (or vice versa).
- Never reuse Infinity portal credentials to gate Kamuk data (same name ≠ same account).
- When rebuilding twins: clone **behavior** from Infinity, rebind **data** + **colors** + **URLs** + **IDs** only.

## Allowed shared pieces (not data mix)

- Static JS/CSS CDN for feature parity (libs).
- Shared AI API host for voice/LLM **when** auth JWT scopes the correct student id and product.

## Rebuild

`node scripts/_archive_kamuk/build-kamuk-twin.mjs` (from Infinity checkout) writes twins into the Kamuk repo without sharing databases.
